            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Be Amazing Dole Whip protein has 20 g of protein per scoop, per the label at the time of writing. The pineapple scoop weighs 37.2 g and the strawberry scoop 35.8 g, so roughly 54 to 56% of the powder is protein. The rest is fiber, MCT oil, fruit juice powder and minerals that give the soft-serve style texture."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Is Be Amazing Dole Whip protein third-party tested?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Be Amazing states on its website that its products are third-party tested, but it does not name a certifier, and we did not find the Dole Whip flavors listed with Informed Sport or NSF Certified for Sport. If you are a tested athlete, the Ascent Pineapple Coconut clear whey on this page is Informed Sport certified, per Ascent."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Is Dole Whip protein powder healthy?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "It is a reasonable protein supplement: 20 g of protein, under 1 g of sugar, 4 g of fiber and no artificial sweeteners, per the label at the time of writing. The trade-offs are 350 to 370 mg of sodium per scoop and a lower protein share than whey isolate. People with kidney disease, high blood pressure or pregnancy should check with a doctor or dietitian."
          }
