            The bag size matters more than the flavor. The pineapple's 15-serving bag is the main reason it costs more per gram than the strawberry, because the formula and protein per scoop are the same. On Be Amazing's own site the 15-serving bags were listed at $39.99 and the 25-serving bags at $49.99 when we checked, which works out to about $3.33 and $2.50 per 25 g. Amazon was cheaper on the day we looked, but prices on both move often, so compare before you buy.
          </p>

          <p>
            Is the Dole Whip premium worth paying? For flavor fans, probably yes: there is no other way to get the licensed taste, and the difference between $2.92 and $1.61 per 25 g is about $1.30 per shake. For someone drinking two shakes a day for a month, though, that gap is closer to $80, and a plain vanilla protein blended with frozen pineapple gets surprisingly close (see the recipe section). Our <a href="/best-cheap-protein-powder/">cheap protein powder guide</a> covers the budget end if cost is the deciding factor.
          </p>

